    <div class="ab-cols ab-after">
      <p>PESM and ARABART 4.15 share 3,298 identical bytes: his glyph tables and his 136-byte joining routine. The routine was right in 1991, and it never needed to change. That same year he also made a <a href={`${base}/program/arabart-commercial/`}>slide show for a Port Said computer center</a>. It was the step before ARABART: its Arabic is stored as short runs of pixels, drawn with a shadow.</p>
      <p>Every Arabic letter on this page, from the title to the typewriter, was drawn by his code. <a href={`${base}/program/arabic-basmallah/`}>Run PESM</a>, <a href={`${base}/program/arabart-demo/`}>the demo</a> or <a href={`${base}/program/brave-sun/`}>The Brave Sun</a> to see it on his own screens.</p>
